TIER E2 CANDIDATES -- "a cell-type identity program unrelated to inflammation"
====================================================================================================
The mouse arm's E2 (hepatocyte identity) FAILED: its score correlated with the zonation
axis at r = -0.67, worse than 99%% of random size-matched sets (genesets/README.md sec 6).
The decisive test for any candidate here is the same correlation against the A6 axis, and
that test NEEDS EXPRESSION -- it is post-freeze. What can be decided now is whether a
candidate is confounded with the A6 axis BY CONSTRUCTION, i.e. whether its own genes are
the compartment definition.

